.TH LBM_TUNNEL 1 "October 2026" "wind-tunnel-2d" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbm_tunnel \- 2D lattice-Boltzmann wind tunnel (BGK, pedagogical)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbm_tunnel
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbm_tunnel
is the lattice-Boltzmann companion to
.BR wind_tunnel (1):
same geometry, same obstacles, same SDL shell, deliberately different
solver. State is the D2Q9 distribution
.IR "f_i(x,t)" ;
collide is single-relaxation-time BGK, stream is pull-scheme with halfway
bounce-back on the solid mask. Viscosity is set by the relaxation time
.RI "nu = c_s^2 (tau \- 1/2)."
.PP
This solver is faithful only in the weakly-compressible subsonic regime.
It is stable through about Mach 0.30 on the cylinder and diverges past Mach
0.40, which is the well-known BGK stability ceiling.
.B That failure is the pedagogical point:
run both this and
.BR wind_tunnel (1)
on the same low-Mach cylinder (they agree), then raise the Mach on each
and watch the LBM fail where the particles keep working.
.PP
For an interactive solver that does
.I not
have that ceiling at the same tolerance, see
.BR lbm_pro (1).
For headless benchmark validation, see
.BR lbm_bench (1).
.SH CONTROLS
Keyboard controls track
.BR wind_tunnel (1)
where they map
.RB ( "SPACE R G O +/\(mi 0 C [ ] L H Q" ).
LBM-specific:
.TP
.B F
Toggle speed vs vorticity colouring (the Karman street is far clearer in
vorticity).
.TP
.B P
Arm a transient symmetry-breaking seed behind the cylinder; a perfectly
symmetric noise-free LBM does not spontaneously shed. Expires in ~400
steps; the HUD shows
.B SEED ON
then
.BR "SEED SPENT" .
.TP
.B V
Toggle MP4 recording (writes
.BR lbm_tunnel_<timestamp>.mp4 ).
.TP
.B "up / down arrow"
Fine-adjust the Mach slider from the keyboard.
.TP
.B "Mouse (drag)"
Two live sliders: INLET MACH (0-0.55) and TAU (0.51-1.50). Releasing a
slider re-initialises the lattice cleanly from the new parameters.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Headless mode (same conventions as the MD):
.TP
.B LB_SELFTEST=1
Run headless.
.TP
.B "LB_STEPS LB_GEOM LB_OBS LB_MACH LB_TAU LB_PERTURB"
Overrides. See
.BR wind_tunnel (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.B ./lbm_tunnel
.RE
.PP
Headless Mach-ceiling probe (expect DIVERGED past about 0.40):
.PP
.RS
.B LB_SELFTEST=1 LB_MACH=0.45 LB_STEPS=5000 ./lbm_tunnel
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wind_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_pro (1),
.BR lbm_bench (1)
